WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:01.980
- I love the cowboy boots!

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:03.570
- I brought a little bit
of Nashville back to you.

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:04.920
- Yes, I love it. I love it.

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:06.060
Meet Awkwafina. Have y'all met before?

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:06.893
- Yes.
- We just did.

00:00:06.893 --> 00:00:08.820
I have not, but I'm a big
fan and I love that letter.

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:10.020
I'm a big fan of that letter.

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:10.860
- Oh, thank you.

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:14.130
- And it also kind of blew me
away because the characters

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:16.839
you often play are so full of confidence.

00:00:16.839 --> 00:00:17.672
- And bold, yeah.

00:00:17.672 --> 00:00:19.117
- And that there's none
of that is in there.

00:00:19.117 --> 00:00:21.180
- It's all a facade.
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:23.962
- Great acting. It's Golden
Globe winning acting.

00:00:23.962 --> 00:00:24.795
- Oh wow.

00:00:24.795 --> 00:00:25.628
- Do you have stuff like
that? Do you journal?

00:00:25.628 --> 00:00:27.180
Do you keep anything and
you find it years later?

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:29.353
- All of my journals end on January 3rd.

00:00:29.353 --> 00:00:30.186
(audience laughing)

00:00:30.186 --> 00:00:33.090
I would ask for diaries and
then on January 1 I'd nail it.

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:34.290
- [Kelly] Gonna kill it.

00:00:35.323 --> 00:00:37.200
- But I have a letter from my wife.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.600
I was up for "Band of Brothers" years ago.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:41.040
And I got so close on it.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.660
I mean all the way up to, literally,

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:45.060
Steven Spielberg with a handy cam

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:47.940
going along like this
in the rehearsal room.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:50.430
And for whatever reason I didn't get it.

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:53.100
And it was a hard one.
It sort of was a crusher.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:54.030
- Oh, when you like really want something.

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:57.390
- She wrote this letter to
me, like, handwritten letter.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:59.340
And all these years later
when I went to Nashville,

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:00.870
it was just saying, "I know this is hard,

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:03.360
but it's a step and you're gonna
be fine," all these things.

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:04.740
And years later, I'm a pack rat,

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:07.020
so we were moving to
Nashville to do that show.

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:08.850
And I looked in there
and I found this thing

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:10.620
and I was like, "Come
on man, that's perfect."

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:13.530
So somebody writes for me I'm grateful.

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:15.090
- That's so sweet. I love your wife.

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:16.170
I love your whole family.

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:18.240
Your family's so cool.
- Oh, they love you.

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:19.764
My sister loves you so much.

00:01:19.764 --> 00:01:20.730
- Oh really?

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:22.140
- I love you, but my sister,

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:24.300
you're not even Kelly Clarkson to her,

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:25.890
you're some Kelly Clarkson to her.

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:28.361
'Cause she says I love
me some Kelly Clarkson.

00:01:28.361 --> 00:01:30.403
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:01:30.403 --> 00:01:32.310
- I see, that must be a southern thing.

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:34.920
Okay, so you've done
well acting in comedies.

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:37.020
So like "The Office", I
know that happened as well.

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:38.370
So how did you end up doing "The Office"?

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:39.277
How did that audition happen?

00:01:39.277 --> 00:01:41.910
- "The Office", I've been
doing normal auditions.

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:43.260
I found out how you really get a job

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:45.630
and that is you have tape of you

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:47.580
and one of the cast members on something.

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:49.620
- Like blackmail?
(audience laughing)

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:50.453
- A little bit like blackmail.

00:01:50.453 --> 00:01:53.490
Rainn Wilson and I, about seven
or eight years before that,

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:56.190
did a pilot called "The Expendables"

00:01:56.190 --> 00:01:59.340
where we played androids
that solved crimes.

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:02.460
And we were, like, robotic but very human.

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:04.800
We spent, I think, a good 30% of it

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:06.300
naked and charging like this.

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:08.280
- Naked and what? (laughs)

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:09.420
- Just shooting above that.

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:12.780
And so when I got there,
I did the whole audition

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:13.897
and one of the producers said,

00:02:13.897 --> 00:02:15.750
"So I understand you're
friends with Rainn."

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:17.940
And I said, "Yeah, did
he tell you how we met?"

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:20.697
And he goes, "No." And
I go, "I bet he didn't."

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:24.870
So I told them and they
were losing their minds

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:27.750
trying to picture Rainn being,
and he was amazing in it.

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:29.827
So funny, but we were, like, talking,

00:02:29.827 --> 00:02:32.520
"I'm starting to have feelings,"
kind of thing like that.

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:34.530
And I said, "So I have
that, but not only that,

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:37.710
if I get this job day
one, I show up with a DVD

00:02:37.710 --> 00:02:39.480
of that pilot that I will give to you."

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:42.390
And I was not even in
my car and my phone rang

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:44.070
and I was like, "Oh, I got the job."

00:02:44.070 --> 00:02:45.516
So, yeah, that's how I got on.

00:02:45.516 --> 00:02:48.499
- Note to self, actors.
(audience applauding)

00:02:48.499 --> 00:02:49.950
Note to self.

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:52.140
Well, Awkwafina, what was
your most memorable audition?

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:53.787
Good or bad.

00:02:53.787 --> 00:02:56.880
- In the early days I went to a thing

00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:00.990
where the reader definitely
passed wind during,

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:03.210
while I was speaking, and I was,

00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:05.070
and I didn't know how to, like, end it.

00:03:05.070 --> 00:03:08.160
I was like, "Did you just hear that?"

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:09.330
And they were like,
"No, I didn't hear that.

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:10.163
Did you hear something?"

00:03:10.163 --> 00:03:11.970
And I was like, but it's
gonna be on the tape that you,

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:12.827
okay, forget it, forget it."

00:03:12.827 --> 00:03:15.166
- So it's gonna look like
you are ripping one. (laughs)

00:03:15.166 --> 00:03:15.999
- It looks like I did it.

00:03:15.999 --> 00:03:16.950
It looks like I had done it

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:18.840
and I didn't stop it
and it just kept going.

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:19.980
- That was your first acting test,

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:21.600
acting like that didn't happen.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:22.710
(audience laughing)

00:03:22.710 --> 00:03:24.810
- Yes, exactly.
- Oh my God.

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:27.420
Okay, so Charles, your latest
project is "Outer Banks."

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:28.977
So what's happening this season?

00:03:28.977 --> 00:03:32.580
(audience cheering)

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:33.870
- It's been so great.

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:36.150
It's been a really great
season for my character.

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:37.590
'Cause he's sort of won all the gold

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:39.000
and all the treasure at
the end of last season

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:40.650
but he really didn't have anything.

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:42.750
Meanwhile the pogues
have nothing, these kids.

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:43.800
But they have each other.

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:46.140
So I sort of hit a rock
bottom and then it's like,

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:48.030
what's gonna happen to the character next?

00:03:48.030 --> 00:03:49.440
But the thing I love most is we shot

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:51.450
so much of it under lockdown,

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:52.860
you know, the quarantining and all that.

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:54.120
And so these kids that,

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:55.710
these younger actors, they're not kids,

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:57.990
but they're so great and
they're so wonderful.

00:03:57.990 --> 00:04:02.130
They sort of blew up under,
you know, the lockdowns.

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:03.180
- In the bubble.
- Yeah, exactly.

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:05.310
And then they were wearing
their masks and so,

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:07.290
but since then, it was really nice.

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:09.030
We just had the premiere, had an event

00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:11.190
with bands onstage and
everything to get to see them

00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:13.800
get all the love from
everybody, it's a thrill.

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:15.990
And people seem to be
loving "Outer Banks" three.

00:04:15.990 --> 00:04:16.823
- I love that.

00:04:16.823 --> 00:04:18.570
People getting their
flowers while they're alive.

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:20.010
That's nice.
- Yeah, exactly.

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:21.093
They deserve it too. They're so cool.

00:04:21.093 --> 00:04:21.926
- Yeah, I love that.

00:04:21.926 --> 00:04:23.640
Well, you're playing your
new song for us later.

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:25.170
So it's called, "One Good Move."

00:04:25.170 --> 00:04:27.436
So what's it about other than,
you know, a solid good move?

00:04:27.436 --> 00:04:28.497
(audience laughing)

00:04:28.497 --> 00:04:32.400
- No, it's not that. It's about my wife.

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:34.980
I was talking with some
songwriters, young songwriters,

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:35.880
and saying I don't envy them,

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:38.250
because, you know, phones
that have video cameras.

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:39.960
Thank God they weren't
around when I was young.

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:42.330
'Cause I was a moron when I was a kid.

00:04:42.330 --> 00:04:43.862
I was a bad decision machine.

00:04:43.862 --> 00:04:46.524
You put in a quarter, I will
give you a bad decision.

00:04:46.524 --> 00:04:47.357
(audience laughing)

00:04:47.357 --> 00:04:48.930
And then I said, "You know
what? Except for one thing.

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:53.400
Somehow that idiot met her and somehow

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:54.810
was smart enough to hang on to her."

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:56.310
And I go, "She was my one good move."

00:04:56.310 --> 00:04:58.530
So when it was time to write
they go, "So that's the title."

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:00.780
And I went, "Ooh, yeah, you're right."

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:01.920
It's actually her birthday today.

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:03.041
- It is?

00:05:03.041 --> 00:05:03.874
- So I get to sing "One Good Move"

00:05:03.874 --> 00:05:05.120
for my one good move on her birthday.

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:06.423
(audience applauding)

00:05:06.423 --> 00:05:07.841
- [Kelly] What is your
life? That is so sweet.

00:05:07.841 --> 00:05:08.880
- [Charles] Right, what is it?

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:10.410
- Okay, we need another break, everybody.

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:12.900
Charles's new song is
called "One Good Move."

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:15.030
And stick around because he's
performing it a little later.

00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:16.130
It's gonna be awesome.

